    "topic": "what sleep tight really means",
    "summary": "The popular story that 'sleep tight' comes from tightening the ropes that supported old mattresses doesn't stand up to scrutiny: the phrase was rare when rope-strung beds were common. 'Tight' meant soundly or properly, so 'sleep tight' meant 'sleep soundly'. The earliest citation found is an 1866 diary entry ('Sleep tight and wake bright'); the OED lists none until 1933.",
    "angle": "Sleep tight just means sleep well.",
